INT. SYNERGY PARTNERS - OPEN OFFICE - MORNING

A sea of gray cubicles. A foosball table nobody uses. A neon sign reads "BE THE CHANGE." A printer in the corner beeps in distress.

DEBORAH PRZYBYLSKI, 40s, regional VP, strides in carrying a laptop and a green smoothie. Behind her trail four employees: SANJAY RAO, 30s; KENDRA OYELOWO, 20s; BRADLEY "BRAD" FITCH, 30s; and a thin man in an ill-fitting suit.

DEBORAH
Team! Huddle!

They gather. The thin man hangs back.

DEBORAH (CONT'D)
Q3 numbers are in. We are crushing it. Crushing. Is anyone not crushing?

Nobody speaks. The printer beeps.

SANJAY
(muttering)
We missed target by thirty percent.

DEBORAH
What was that?

SANJAY
I said we're... trending.

DEBORAH
Good word. Trending.

KENDRA
(to Brad)
Who is that guy?

BRAD
(whispering)
HR, I think.

KENDRA
He's been here an hour.

BRAD
He's been in the printer room.

DEBORAH
Team. I want to introduce someone.

She gestures at the thin man, who steps forward and clutches his clipboard.

DEBORAH (CONT'D)
This is Mr. Lyle, from Corporate.

MR. LYLE
Hello.

DEBORAH
Mr. Lyle is here to help us optimize.

MR. LYLE
I'm here to make cuts.

Silence. Deborah's smile does not move. Sanjay's eyes widen. Kendra covers her mouth. Brad slowly raises his hand.

BRAD
Is that a joke?

MR. LYLE
No.

DEBORAH
It's a figure of speech.

MR. LYLE
It is not.

DEBORAH
(through teeth)
Mr. Lyle, may I have a word.

MR. LYLE
Certainly.

They step aside. The three employees watch. Lyle speaks, quietly, and Deborah's face cracks. She snatches her smoothie, takes a long pull through the straw, and, finding it empty, sucks on air.

Lyle returns, alone. Deborah remains by the foosball table, staring at it.

MR. LYLE (CONT'D)
Ms. Przybylski has decided to take personal leave.

SANJAY
Indefinitely?

MR. LYLE
Effective immediately.

KENDRA
(simultaneously)
Who's in charge?

^BRAD
(simultaneously)
Who's in charge?

Lyle looks at them. He glances at the clipboard.

MR. LYLE
Mr. Rao.

SANJAY
Me?

MR. LYLE
Congratulations. You're trending.
